Subject: [PATCH] main: read /etc/daynight.state sidecar in main() (not CFG::load) + run crash handler on a sigaltstack
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (stacks on 0001-0014)

The two MQTT-frequent modes (auto/day/night) persist in a tiny atomic sidecar
/etc/daynight.state ("mode=auto|day|night"), written by the rootfs helper
/usr/sbin/daynight-state. prudynt reads it directly so the selected mode survives
reboot WITHOUT the full ~8.5KB non-atomic prudynt.json rewrite.

WHY IN main() AND NOT IN CFG::load():
An earlier revision read the sidecar INSIDE CFG::load() (after the prudynt.json
item loops). That crashed prudynt at startup with a SIGSEGV inside libuclibcshim
(the T23 glibc->uClibc ABI shim), faulting at the TOP OF THE STACK -- and it
crashed identically with every I/O form tried (ifstream / fopen / raw open) and
even with the sidecar file absent. The C++ logic itself is sound and memory-safe:
force_mode_cfg already takes a .rodata string literal as its item-table default,
so assigning "day"/"night"/"" literals is the existing ownership contract and
nothing ever frees it. The crash was a code-emission / frame effect -- folding
the read (and its locals) into the already-enormous CFG::load() perturbed that
function's stack-frame / unwind layout enough to trip the ABI shim on re-entry.
Moving the read into a SEPARATE noinline function with its OWN frame, called from
main() right after the config is constructed, keeps CFG::load() byte-identical to
the proven build and resolves the crash while preserving the direct-read design.
(noinline matters: at -O2 a once-called static would be inlined into main(),
re-introducing the same frame perturbation there; noinline guarantees isolation.)

Timing is correct: the override runs after CFG::load() (so it wins over any
prudynt.json value) and before IMPSystem::createNew() (patch 0001) derives the ISP
running_mode from force_mode_cfg at main.cpp:605 -- nothing between make_shared and
that point reads running_mode/force_mode_cfg. The read is allocation-free (raw
open/read, C buffers, static literals) so it adds no malloc/free or std::string
cleanup region.

Also folds in the crash-handler hardening (previously a separate diagnostic): the
SIGSEGV/SIGABRT/... handler now runs on a sigaltstack (SA_ONSTACK) so it survives
a stack-overflow fault and can still write /tmp/prudynt_crash.log. This is a
permanent robustness improvement and the safety net should any startup fault
recur -- the next crash, if any, produces a register+backtrace report instead of
being invisible.

Verified: git apply --check + patch -p1 both pass against f4b3228 + 0001-0014.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 2b35d77..00db3c2 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -494,6 +494,58 @@ void start_video(int encChn) {
   sh.has_started.acquire();
 }

+// Read the persisted day/night mode from the /etc/daynight.state sidecar and
+// apply it to the already-loaded config. Deliberately a SEPARATE function with
+// its OWN small stack frame, called from main() AFTER CFG::load() has run --
+// NOT folded into CFG::load(). Adding this read (and its locals) into the very
+// large CFG::load() perturbed that function's frame/unwind layout enough to trip
+// the T23 uClibc ABI shim at startup (SIGSEGV inside libuclibcshim, faulting at
+// the top of the stack), even though the C++ logic itself is sound. Kept
+// allocation-free: raw open/read (no fopen/filebuf), C buffers (no std::string),
+// and static string literals (no malloc/free) -- force_mode_cfg already takes a
+// .rodata literal as its default, so this matches the existing ownership.
+// noinline is deliberate: it guarantees this read gets its OWN stack frame at -O2
+// (a once-called static would otherwise be inlined into main()), keeping the
+// frame/unwind perturbation that crashed CFG::load() out of main() too.
+__attribute__((noinline)) static void
+apply_daynight_sidecar(const std::shared_ptr<CFG> &c) {
+  if (!c)
+    return;
+  char buf[64];
+  ssize_t n = -1;
+  int fd = ::open("/etc/daynight.state", O_RDONLY);
+  if (fd >= 0) {
+    n = ::read(fd, buf, sizeof(buf) - 1);
+    ::close(fd);
+  }
+  buf[(n > 0) ? (size_t)n : 0] = '\0';
+
+  // locate mode=<value>, skip an optional quote/space, read the lowercase token
+  char mode[8];
+  size_t mi = 0;
+  const char *mp = std::strstr(buf, "mode=");
+  if (mp) {
+    mp += 5;
+    while (*mp == '"' || *mp == ' ' || *mp == '\t' || *mp == '\r' ||
+           *mp == '\n')
+      ++mp;
+    while (mi < sizeof(mode) - 1 && *mp >= 'a' && *mp <= 'z')
+      mode[mi++] = *mp++;
+  }
+  mode[mi] = '\0';
+
+  if (std::strcmp(mode, "night") == 0) {
+    c->daynight.enabled = false;
+    c->daynight.force_mode_cfg = "night";
+  } else if (std::strcmp(mode, "day") == 0) {
+    c->daynight.enabled = false;
+    c->daynight.force_mode_cfg = "day";
+  } else {
+    c->daynight.enabled = true;
+    c->daynight.force_mode_cfg = "";
+  }
+}
+
 int main(int argc, const char *argv[]) {
   if (Logger::init("INFO")) {
     LOG_ERROR("Logger initialization failed.");
@@ -530,12 +582,25 @@ int main(int argc, const char *argv[]) {

   // Install crash signal handlers to clean up lock file and collect diagnostics
   // on abnormal termination
+  // DIAGNOSTIC: run the crash handler on a dedicated alternate stack
+  // (SA_ONSTACK). Without this the handler cannot execute when the fault is a
+  // stack overflow (the kernel can't push the signal frame onto an exhausted
+  // stack), so no /tmp/prudynt_crash.log is produced and the crash is invisible.
+  // With an alt stack the handler runs and writes the register/backtrace report
+  // regardless of fault type.
+  static char crash_alt_stack[32768];
+  stack_t crash_ss;
+  crash_ss.ss_sp = crash_alt_stack;
+  crash_ss.ss_size = sizeof(crash_alt_stack);
+  crash_ss.ss_flags = 0;
+  sigaltstack(&crash_ss, nullptr);
+
   struct sigaction sa;
   memset(&sa, 0, sizeof(sa));
   sa.sa_sigaction = crash_signal_handler_extended;
   sigemptyset(&sa.sa_mask);
-  sa.sa_flags = SA_SIGINFO | SA_RESETHAND; // Get detailed signal info, reset to
-                                           // default after first invocation
+  sa.sa_flags = SA_SIGINFO | SA_RESETHAND | SA_ONSTACK; // detailed info; reset to
+                                           // default after first; run on altstack

   sigaction(SIGSEGV, &sa, nullptr); // Segmentation fault
   sigaction(SIGABRT, &sa, nullptr); // Abort signal
@@ -575,6 +640,10 @@ int main(int argc, const char *argv[]) {
   recover_stale_imp_state();

   cfg = std::make_shared<CFG>();
+  // Override day/night from the persisted sidecar BEFORE anything consumes it
+  // (IMPSystem::init derives running_mode from force_mode_cfg). Done here, not in
+  // CFG::load(), to keep that function's frame/ABI identical to the proven build.
+  apply_daynight_sidecar(cfg);
   Logger::setLevel(cfg->general.loglevel);

 #if defined(WEBSOCKET_ENABLED)
